tedge-dot patch for net-snmp 5.9.4 (applied by impl/c/CMakeLists.txt with `patch -p1`)

The SNMP connector decodes notifications and responses with libnetsnmp, and both
implementations are held to connectors/snmp/conformance/trap-vectors.json
(doc/connectors/snmp-connector-spec.md §4.2, §8). Stock 5.9.4 disagrees with those
vectors where it is lenient in ways the connector cannot see after the fact, because
the information is gone once the value is stored:

1. asn_parse_int truncates an INTEGER wider than 32 bits (CHECK_OVERFLOW_S), so an
   eight-octet INTEGER decodes as 0. The full value is kept (LP64; an ILP32 long
   still rejects more than four octets).
2. asn_parse_unsigned_int accepts up to sizeof(long)+1 octets and truncates a
   Counter32/Gauge32/TimeTicks above 2^32-1. It now requires 1-5 octets and a
   value of at most 2^32-1: an error, not a truncation (spec §4.2).
3. asn_parse_objid decodes an empty OID (06 00) as 0.0. It is now an error.
4. snmp_parse_var_op stops after a VarBind's value, so an element after the value
   inside the VarBind is parsed as the next VarBind and the whole message fails.
   It now skips to the end of the VarBind SEQUENCE (spec §4.1: ignored).
5. snmp_pdu_parse accepts any string-typed agent-addr of up to four octets in a
   v1 Trap-PDU. It now requires an IpAddress of exactly four octets.

6. sc_encrypt/sc_decrypt implement AES only for a real OpenSSL
   (#if defined(NETSNMP_USE_OPENSSL) && defined(HAVE_AES)), so with
   --with-openssl=internal an AES-128 user matches no branch at all: the scoped
   PDU is sent UNENCRYPTED with the privacy flag set, sc_encrypt reports
   success, and no peer can parse the message. The bundled crypto already
   carries AES CFB-128 (snmplib/openssl/openssl_aes_cfb.c), so the branch is
   added for the internal build too. Without this, the C connector supports DES
   privacy only -- which contradicts spec §10 and the packaged configuration.

Everything else the vectors require of a notification (PDU kinds per version, the
trap OID derivation, generic/specific-trap ranges, 128 arcs, 256 varbinds) is
connector-owned (§4.3) and checked in impl/c/connectors/snmp/snmp_netsnmp.c.

